From 765fadb802a6c733aa60cb6362424c63d8ae0a75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:36:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mcp): the cli refuses a ui link peer that does not prove
 the token

A crashed window leaves its discovery file behind, and on Windows the
CLI opened a session with any peer on that stale port that answered
HELLO_OK - the peer never proved that it read the file. Three closes:

- The client sends a nonce in its hello; the window answers with a
  proof (two FNV-1a 64-bit words over token and nonce, no new crypto
  dependency) and the client refuses a peer whose answer does not
  prove it. A plain hello (an older CLI) still gets plain HELLO_OK.
- Before it connects, the CLI checks that the pid in the file is
  alive (kill on Unix, OpenProcess on Windows) and removes the file of
  a dead pid - never a live window's file.
- The answer reads are bounded: one answer line at 1 MiB, a bridge
  session at 256 MiB; the HELLO_TIMEOUT deadline covers the whole
  proof exchange.

Pinned by ui_link::a_false_window_that_does_not_prove_the_token_gets_no_tool_call.

Fixes #3874
